      "id": "prop:hms-class-inclusion",
      "change": "changed",
      "fields": [
        "statement"
      ],
      "content": true,
      "reasons": [
        "narrow: The frozen off-diagonal condition alone does not control an unobservable diagonal. In the smallest counterexample, take \\(K=1\\), one positive-probability assignment with \\(O_z=\\varnothing\\), and \\(H=[1]\\). The stated distinct-pair condition is vacuous, but \\(h_H(\\theta)=\\theta_0\\notin\\mathcal E_{\\mathcal J}\\), which contains only constants. Requiring a zero diagonal exactly for never-observed coordinates is the minimal missing observability condition; it is vacuous in the six-coordinate witness, where every singleton is observed."
      ]
    }
